---
/*
 * "Report a problem" and "For coding agents" (`llms.txt`), under every page,
 * laid out as the next/previous links under them are: at either edge, each
 * label after a line icon of the arrows' size, so the labels line up.
 *
 * There's no "Edit page" link: the source repository is private.
 *
 * "Report a problem" starts an email to contact@kindgi.com, its subject
 * naming the page and its body the page's address.
 *
 * `llms.txt` lists every page's Markdown version, for an agent to read.
 *
 * Search leaves the row out: it's the same on every page.
 */
import { Icon } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

const CONTACT = 'contact@kindgi.com';

const route = Astro.locals.starlightRoute;

const page = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, 'https://docs.kindgi.com').href;
// Percent-encoded, not a query string's `+`, with CRLF line breaks: mail
// apps read RFC 6068.
const subject = encodeURIComponent(`Docs: ${route.entry.data.title}`);
const body = encodeURIComponent(`Page: ${page}\r\n\r\n`);
const report = `mailto:${CONTACT}?subject=${subject}&body=${body}`;

const llms = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/')}llms.txt`;
---

<div class="kindgi-page-links sl-flex print:hidden" data-pagefind-ignore>
  <a href={report} class="sl-flex">
    <Icon name="comment-alt" size="1rem" />
    Report a problem
  </a>
  <a href={llms} class="sl-flex">
    <Icon name="list-format" size="1rem" />
    For coding agents
  </a>
</div>

<style>
  .kindgi-page-links {
    flex-grow: 1;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  a {
    gap: 0.375rem;
    align-items: center;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
  a:hover {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
</style>
